From: furiosa <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 16:31:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 52/63] fix(dolt): reap orphaned embedded sql-server processes
 (gfork-d5h)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operational orphan-process reaper: gt dolt cleanup --processes (manual,
--dry-run supported) terminates operationally-orphaned dolt sql-server
processes (reparented to init or rooted in an ephemeral data dir, no live
client connections). Never touches the bastion/production server (3307 /
bastion data dir protected — see TestShouldReapOrphanCandidate). Addresses
the 26-leaked-embedded-server incident (hq-wisp-8ww).

RESCUE: this is gfork/furiosa's completed gfork-d5h work. Its polecat branch
was cut off the old anvil tip (2b5f247f) and stranded un-rebasable by the
fork-baseline resync (81233d36 -> 5ffa55a2); the unpushed work was rescued
by replaying its net 2b5f247f..5cfbda01 diff onto current anvil. Reaper tests
pass on the new baseline; pre-existing EnsureAllMetadata failures tracked
separately (gfork-oz2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
